  "segments": [
   {
    "id": "t1",
    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 3.82,
    "text": "The Maha Minutes, we're going to rewind time and we're going to think back the last five"
   },
   {
    "id": "t2",
    "start": 3.82,
    "end": 8.68,
    "text": "years in COVID and what was the country that had some of the most strict mandates when"
   },
   {
    "id": "t3",
    "start": 8.68,
    "end": 10.52,
    "text": "it came to vaccines?"
   },
   {
    "id": "t4",
    "start": 10.52,
    "end": 11.52,
    "text": "It was Australia."
   },
   {
    "id": "t5",
    "start": 11.52,
    "end": 17.12,
    "text": "Well, there's a new study coming out of Australia among 30 to 40-year-olds and their cancer"
   },
   {
    "id": "t6",
    "start": 17.12,
    "end": 18.12,
    "text": "rates."
   },
   {
    "id": "t7",
    "start": 18.12,
    "end": 19.48,
    "text": "And here's what they have found."
   },
   {
    "id": "t8",
    "start": 19.48,
    "end": 23.76,
    "text": "Over the last five years and typically healthy 30 to 40-year-olds, prostate cancer is up"
   },
   {
    "id": "t9",
    "start": 23.76,
    "end": 25.52,
    "text": "a whopping 500 percent."
   },
   {
    "id": "t10",
    "start": 25.52,
    "end": 27.32,
    "text": "Nope, that's not what they found."
   },
   {
    "id": "t11",
    "start": 27.32,
    "end": 28.88,
    "text": "She's lying to spread propaganda."
   },
   {
    "id": "t12",
    "start": 28.88,
    "end": 33.52,
    "text": "The data showing prostate cancer at 500% in men 30 to 39 and increases in other cancer"
   },
   {
    "id": "t13",
    "start": 33.52,
    "end": 39.38,
    "text": "from Australia is actually from the years 2000 to 2024, 25 years of data."
   },
   {
    "id": "t14",
    "start": 39.38,
    "end": 42.62,
    "text": "She chopped off two decades to sell you a conspiratorial story."
   },
   {
    "id": "t15",
    "start": 42.62,
    "end": 43.62,
    "text": "You can't do that."
   },
   {
    "id": "t16",
    "start": 43.62,
    "end": 47.56,
    "text": "You can't pretend that a 25 year increase is actually a 5 year increase and then choose"
   },
   {
    "id": "t17",
    "start": 47.56,
    "end": 51.9,
    "text": "a random variable that correlates with your fake data range to imply causation."
   },
   {
    "id": "t18",
    "start": 51.9,
    "end": 52.9,
    "text": "That's propaganda."
   },
   {
    "id": "t19",
    "start": 52.9,
    "end": 56.0,
    "text": "Scientists from around the world who are actually studying these trends point to things"
   },
   {
    "id": "t20",
    "start": 56.0,
    "end": 60.88,
    "text": "like improved screening, obesity trends, infections, and environmental exposures."
   },
   {
    "id": "t21",
    "start": 60.88,
    "end": 64.92,
    "text": "The Australian reporting that she misused literally quotes researchers talking about"
   },
   {
    "id": "t22",
    "start": 64.92,
    "end": 68.76,
    "text": "things like the exbosome and environmental drivers, not vaccines."
   },
   {
    "id": "t23",
    "start": 68.76,
    "end": 72.76,
    "text": "And the drivers that they mentioned are things like PFOS, or forever chemicals, and other"
   },
   {
    "id": "t24",
    "start": 72.76,
    "end": 76.6,
    "text": "environmental contaminants, which makes it even worse that this administration rolled"
   },
   {
    "id": "t25",
    "start": 76.6,
    "end": 81.72,
    "text": "back PFOS drinking water standards and announced an aggressive rollback of environmental regulation"
   },
   {
    "id": "t26",
    "start": 81.72,
    "end": 83.84,
    "text": "that helps polluting industries."
   },
   {
    "id": "t27",
    "start": 83.84,
    "end": 88.66,
    "text": "If vaccines were causing increased cancer rates, independent researchers worldwide would"
   },
   {
    "id": "t28",
    "start": 88.66,
    "end": 89.66,
    "text": "say so."
   },
   {
    "id": "t29",
    "start": 89.66,
    "end": 94.94,
    "text": "Consensus science does not care about industry profits, and it's often inconvenient to industry."
   },
   {
    "id": "t30",
    "start": 94.94,
    "end": 98.86,
    "text": "When evidence showed that lead in paint and gasoline harmed children, independent scientists"
   },
   {
    "id": "t31",
    "start": 98.86,
    "end": 102.82,
    "text": "globally said it and kept saying it, even as industry pushed back."
   },
   {
    "id": "t32",
    "start": 102.82,
    "end": 107.1,
    "text": "And when evidence showed that trans fat increased heart disease risk, independent scientists"
   },
   {
    "id": "t33",
    "start": 107.1,
    "end": 110.9,
    "text": "globally said it and kept saying it, even as industry pushed back."
   },
   {
    "id": "t34",
    "start": 110.9,
    "end": 115.58,
    "text": "If vaccines caused all of the issues that these influencers and anti-vaxxers say that"
   },
   {
    "id": "t35",
    "start": 115.58,
    "end": 119.9,
    "text": "they do, scientists from around the world would say it and keep saying it."
   },
   {
    "id": "t36",
    "start": 119.9,
    "end": 121.58,
    "text": "But they don't because it's not true."
   },
   {
    "id": "t37",
    "start": 121.58,
    "end": 125.68,
    "text": "And if it were true, people like this wouldn't have to lie about their data and chop off"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38",
    "start": 125.68,
    "end": 129.74,
    "text": "two decades of a data set in order to spin their conspiratorial story."
   },
   {
    "id": "t39",
    "start": 129.74,
    "end": 135.42,
    "text": "And let's realize that a pro-industry administration benefits when you're distracted by fake vaccine"
   },
   {
    "id": "t40",
    "start": 135.42,
    "end": 136.42,
    "text": "conspiracies."
   },
   {
    "id": "t41",
    "start": 136.42,
    "end": 139.86,
    "text": "Because while you're busy looking at fake vaccine data, they're rolling back environmental"
   },
   {
    "id": "t42",
    "start": 139.86,
    "end": 144.7,
    "text": "regulations for their industry buddies and cutting scientific research funding to cancer"
   },
   {
    "id": "t43",
    "start": 144.7,
    "end": 148.02,
    "text": "and chemical toxicology research, and that's exactly how they want it."
   }
  ]
 },
